rink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.2458425131210711,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.08609,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":57.4,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Hut 8 Corp., together with its subsidiaries, operates as an energy infrastructure platform that integrates power, digital infrastructure, and compute at scale to fuel energy-intensive use cases in the United States and Canada. It operates through Power, Digital Infrastructure, Compute, and Other segments. The company offers managed services for energy infrastructure development, such as site design, procurement, and construction management; software automation, process design, personnel hiring, and team training; utilities contracts, hosting operations, and customer management; energy portfolio optimization and strategic initiatives; and finance, accounting, and safety services. It also engages in the operation of compute infrastructure; and provision, hosting, monitoring, troubleshooting, repair, maintenance, and sale of mining equipment. In addition, the company offers Bitcoin mining; data center and cloud infrastructure services, including colocation services; and ASIC compute, traditional cloud, and AI cloud services. Hut 8 Corp. was founded in 2020 and is based in Miami, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Asher Kevin Genoot | Co-Founder, CEO & Non-Independent Director | Age 29 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 248 people. Revenue per employee of $948K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. Stock-based compensation of $233K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Hut 8 Corp. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $6.9B market cap on $235M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +45% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, thin -10.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 25% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 8.6% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (17.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 166% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $15.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 366% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Hut 8 (HUT) Posts Strong Q3 Results, Is The Stock Now Too Expensive?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/software/nasdaq-hut/hut-8/news/hut-8-hut-posts-strong-q3-results-is-the-stock-now-too-expen","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794514809.002,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.964,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Hut 8: 3 Key Takeaways for Long-Term Investors","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/hut-8-3-key-takeaways-203702384.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794429422.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.188,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Hut 8 Jumps 9%, MARA Rallies 8% Despite Analyst Cuts; Riot Platforms Rises 2% Despite Downgrade","source":"247wallst.com","link":"https://247wallst.com/investing/2026/11/11/hut-8-jumps-9-mara-rallies-8-despite-analyst-cuts-riot-platforms-rises-2-despite-downgrade/","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794423783.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.48,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Why Is Hut 8 Stock Up on Wednesday?","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/11/63144897/why-is-hut-8-stock-up-on-wednesday","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794410871.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Research Analysts Set Expectations for Hut 8 FY2026 Earnings","source":"thelinc